<title>USA: North Carolina food tax cut clears full House.</title>
<headline>North Carolina food tax cut clears full House.</headline>
<dateline>RALEIGH, N.C. 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Carolina's House of Representatives overwhelmingly approved a proposal to cut the state sales tax on food to two percent from three percent.</p>
<p>The proposal passed 106-6 Wednesday and now heads to the Senate.</p>
<p>It would reduce state revenues by about $90 million annually and would take effect Jan 1, 1998. The House approved it after learning that state revenues were running $219 million above projections for the current year.</p>
<p>Last year the General Assembly cut the statewide sales tax on food to three percent from four percent.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
